    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering NoSQL Options**\n\nI'm currently evaluating managed NoSQL options for this Python script. AWS DynamoDB and Google Cloud Firestore seem like strong contenders. The key is to select one and ensure its identity is clear within the `fetch_document.py` code. I need to consider factors like cost, scalability, and ease of integration before I lock in a choice.\n\n\n**Choosing Firestore as Solution**\n\nI've decided to go with Google Cloud Firestore. I plan to directly write the `fetch_document.py` file content using the `write` tool. This file will import the Firestore client library, initialize the client, and define a document-fetching function. Provider-specific identifiers, like `google.cloud.firestore`, will be included to make the database choice clear.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
