    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Implementation**\n\nI'm currently focused on determining the right external provider for the upsert operation. My objective is to build a `upsert_document.py` Python script that efficiently upserts a JSON document using a primary identifier. I need to make sure the chosen provider is clearly identified in the code.\n\n\n**Choosing MongoDB Atlas**\n\nI've decided to move forward with MongoDB Atlas for the upsert operation, focusing on a Python script named `upsert_document.py`. The plan includes using the `pymongo` library for connection and upsert functionality. I'll make sure the connection details and collection name are configurable, perhaps via environment variables. The code will contain provider-specific elements such as the `pymongo` import and the connection string, clearly marked as placeholders to be filled by the user.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789867046777,
          "start": 1789867041294
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc63a20e001PlwhVTHTzALhzc",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc639d020014Ugq6FtzwxIUw4",
